# SDD System Design Patterns

## When triggered
- User asks about architecture
- Designing new aggregates or bounded contexts
- Performance or scalability concerns
- Database schema design

## Decision trees

### Database: {{database}}
### Caching: {{caching}}
### Auth: {{auth}}

### Aggregate boundaries
```
Must change together atomically?
├── YES → Same aggregate
├── NO  → Different aggregates (reference by ID)
├── >10 entities → Split it
```

### Entity vs Value Object
```
Has persistent unique identity?
├── YES → Entity
├── NO  → Value Object (immutable)
```

## Anti-patterns to avoid
- Anemic domain model (entities as data bags)
- Repository per table (should be per aggregate)
- Leaking infrastructure into domain
- Cross-aggregate transactions (use events)
